# peachOS vendor dconf defaults -- applied to every user account (including the one
# Calamares creates during install) via /etc/dconf/db/local.d + `dconf update`, per the
# standard GNOME mechanism for shipping default settings distro-wide. NOT seeded through
# /etc/skel (no per-user file copying needed -- dconf's own system-db layering applies this
# to every user automatically, present or future).
#
# Rebuilt from a full live-session `dconf dump /` (not hand-guessed) the first time anyone
# actually checked whether this file matched the live desktop before a snapshot -- it
# didn't, badly: favorite-apps/enabled-extensions/wallpaper were all stale (an older
# in-progress state, predating this session's dock-extension swap to
# macos-dock-2026-peachos and lockscreen swap to perfect-lockscreen), and the previous
# capture had never been refreshed since. Two real bugs found and fixed while rebuilding it,
# not carried forward:
#
# Re-synced a second time (2026-08-31, ahead of a fresh remaster) after actually diffing
# every key here against live `dconf read`, not assuming the previous sync still held --
# it didn't: color-scheme/user-theme/wallpaper had drifted to dark mode + the Nectar
# wallpaper (Phase 8 of this session's own work, never synced back here), liquid-glass-mode
# and liquid-glass-intensity had both been retuned live during this session's own testing,
# app-picker-layout was missing the installer launcher, and enabled-extensions had a
# harmless but real order difference. All eight fixed to match live exactly.
#   - perfect-lockscreen's lockscreen-wallpaper-path pointed at a /tmp scratchpad test file
#     that wouldn't exist on any other machine -- disabled the custom-photo override here so
#     it correctly falls back to the (real, shipped) rolling-hills.mp4 video background.
#   - media-keys custom-keybindings referenced a 'peachos-test' path with no actual
#     binding/command/name defined anywhere -- a dangling reference that would have shown
#     a broken custom shortcut in Settings. Dropped, kept only the real peachySearch one.
#
# Deliberately excluded: anything that's session/hardware state rather than a peachOS
# "look" default -- window positions/recent-files/notification-history, keyboard layout and
# touchpad/keyboard hardware prefs (a fresh install picks its own via Calamares' own
# locale/keyboard steps, not a baked default), and the disabled/superseded lockscreen
# extensions' (live-lockscreen, wack-lockscreen-clock) own leftover settings.

